                <pb facs="0453" n="329" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg329"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.48/417: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner at Constantinople</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-03-29T15:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 29,
                                1923—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:05 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>86. My 82, March 28, 5 p.m. Destroyer at Mersina reports that local authorities
                    state permission has been obtained from Angora to allow refugees to remain there
                    until transportation becomes available. This revokes threat of death [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">deportation?</hi>] to the interior.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bristol</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
